## 17. TESTING AND VALIDATION

The following tests are mandatory.

Course management:
- Instructor can create a course.
- Instructor can add concepts.
- Instructor can attach text lessons and video links.
- Instructor can edit concepts.

Enrollment:
- Learner can enroll in a course.
- Learner can access available lessons.
- Progress is persisted.

Graph:
- Concepts display correctly.
- Prerequisite links display correctly.
- Valid edges are accepted.
- Cycle-producing edges are rejected.
- Clear cycle explanations are shown.

Mastery:
- Quiz scores are calculated correctly.
- Threshold is configurable.
- A concept unlocks only after all prerequisites are mastered.
- Locked concepts show missing prerequisites.

Learning path:
- Target concept can be selected.
- Required prerequisites are identified.
- Already mastered concepts are skipped.
- Concepts are ordered correctly.
- Estimated learning time is correct.
- Path updates after progress changes.

Curriculum restructuring:
- Prerequisite links can be added and removed.
- Concepts can be split.
- Existing progress is preserved.
- Quiz history is preserved.
- Unlocking is recalculated.
- Learning paths are regenerated.
- Affected learners receive notifications.
- Curriculum history is recorded.

Multilingual:
- English works.
- Kannada works.
- Hindi works.
- Language selection persists.
- No major interface text remains untranslated.

Do not mark a feature complete simply because its page or button exists. Verify the underlying functionality.

